  "measurement_limits": [
    "Three accepted cold boots after provisioning using the same combined fastboot/no-camera image and retained custom minimal R39.2.1 UEFI/QSPI. No image or firmware changes were made for this Ethernet experiment; generated full UEFI is not qualified.",
    "Initial peer carrier was observed below 6 seconds from SCPI command send in every run, then dropped once and recovered in every run. Continuous link is required, so the current profile does not meet the requirement. POST checks remain unspecified.",
    "The electrical input-power edge and physical link edge were not measured. SCPI command/output latency, approximately 2-second board POR holdoff, peer PHY/driver reporting, USB delivery and host scheduling/read latency remain included. No POR estimate was subtracted.",
    "The requested carrier polling interval is 20 ms. Per-run sample counts, maximum completion gaps from the reference through the final read, maximum read durations, every observed transition and final sample time are retained. These gaps do not bound PHY/driver reporting latency; short down/up transitions between samples can be missed.",
    "Final link qualification reports 1000 Mb/s full duplex after the three runs; speed and duplex at each first carrier sample were not measured. Carrier is not IP readiness, successful authentication, application readiness or completion of POST.",
    "C7 remains enabled at Gen2 in Linux; no PCIe FFC endpoint or camera was attached. Attached-endpoint and camera-enabled operation require separate qualification.",
    "Quiet logging produced no observable Linux-start banners. Distinct qualification boot identifiers were checked privately, but the UART banner heuristic cannot exclude an unobservable intervening restart.",
    "CUDA readiness verifies a 65,536-element integer computation, not model loading or inference-server readiness. SSH is a banner-only observation on the separate USB gadget; UART is a normal login prompt without authentication.",
    "Reported Linux uptime and host UART chunk-receive times use different clocks. Their subtraction supplies an approximate diagnostic alignment affected by uptime rounding and marker/UART delivery, not a calibrated clock conversion or causal proof."
  ]
